    "description": "LA Wire covers Los Angeles business, culture and the people building on the West Coast. What it is and how to get featured.",
    "body": "<p>Los Angeles is a market people pay attention to — creative, commercial and unusually well covered.</p>\n<p>Here is what LA Wire is and how people get featured.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-la-wire-is\">What LA Wire is</h2>\n<p>LA Wire is a digital publication covering business, culture, entrepreneurship and lifestyle with a Los Angeles focus. Online only, permanently live, and indexed by search engines.</p>\n<p>It sits in the space where business and creative industries overlap, which is a useful place to be if your brand lives in either.</p>\n<h2 id=\"why-a-los-angeles-dateline-works\">Why a Los Angeles dateline works</h2>\n<p>Place is positioning.</p>\n<p>Los Angeles carries associations no other city does — creative industries, consumer brands, media, wellness, entertainment. A feature tied to that market frames you differently than a generic business profile would, especially if you sell to consumers or work anywhere near culture.</p>\n<p>It also travels. Readers everywhere recognise what an LA story signals.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-a-feature-includes\">What a feature includes</h2>\n<p>A solo, dedicated article about you and your work, with a headline and angle built around your positioning. Typically photos and links to your website, LinkedIn and socials.</p>\n<p>It publishes permanently and stays indexed, so it keeps working every time someone searches your name.</p>\n<h2 id=\"how-to-get-featured\">How to get featured</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Pitch directly.</strong> Free and legitimate, dependent on fit and editorial capacity.</li><li><strong>Use a professional feature service.</strong> A team writes it to the publication's standard and places it. Faster and more predictable, which is why most founders choose it.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"what-makes-a-strong-piece\">What makes a strong piece</h2>\n<p>LA Wire's readers respond to stories with texture.</p>\n<p>That means the specifics: what you are building, who it is for, what you have learned, and why it belongs in this market. A brand story with a real point of view will always outperform a list of achievements.</p>\n<p>If there is a genuine Los Angeles connection — where you operate, who you serve, a partnership, a launch — lead with it.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-to-expect-from-the-process\">What to expect from the process</h2>\n<p>Share your story, our team drafts the piece, you review with revisions until it is exactly right, and nothing publishes until you approve it. Then it goes live and you get the link to share.</p>\n<p>Any provider who cannot show you the draft first is not one to use.</p>\n<h2 id=\"getting-started\">Getting started</h2>\n<p>Digital Networking Agency works with LA Wire and a wide network of digital publications. We write, edit and place. You keep full editorial control, and nothing goes live without your sign-off.</p>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Do I need to be based in Los Angeles?</h3>\n<p>No. A genuine connection to the market helps — clients, partners, a launch, a trend you are seeing — but plenty of featured founders operate elsewhere.</p>\n<h3>What kind of businesses fit LA Wire?</h3>\n<p>Consumer brands, creative and media businesses, wellness, hospitality and founders whose work has a cultural angle tend to fit most naturally.</p>\n<h3>Can I approve the article before it publishes?</h3>\n<p>Yes. You review and revise until it is right, and nothing publishes without your approval.</p>",
