    "slug": "how-to-get-featured-in-us-reporter",
    "h1": "How to Get Featured in US Reporter",
    "title": "How to Get Featured in US Reporter | DNA PR",
    "description": "US Reporter covers business, people and stories across the US. What it is, what a feature includes, and how to get featured.",
    "body": "<p>If your customers are spread across the country rather than concentrated in one market, a national story frame serves you better than a local one.</p>\n<p>Here is what US Reporter is and how people get featured.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-us-reporter-is\">What US Reporter is</h2>\n<p>US Reporter is an independent digital publication covering business, entrepreneurship and human-interest stories across the United States. Online only, permanently live, and indexed by search engines.</p>\n<p>One clarification worth making: several publications use similar names. This is usreporter.com, an independent digital title — not affiliated with any national broadcaster or wire service.</p>\n<h2 id=\"why-a-national-frame-matters\">Why a national frame matters</h2>\n<p>Where you are covered shapes how far the story reaches.</p>\n<p>A regional feature tells a reader you matter in one place. A national frame tells them your work is not bounded by geography — which is the right signal if you sell online, operate remotely, or serve customers in multiple states.</p>\n<p>It is also more useful as a general-purpose credibility asset. Nobody has to know the city to understand the coverage.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-a-feature-includes\">What a feature includes</h2>\n<p>A solo, dedicated article about you and your work, with a headline and angle built around your positioning. Typically photos and links to your website, LinkedIn and socials.</p>\n<p>It publishes permanently and stays indexed, becoming a reference point every time someone researches you.</p>\n<h2 id=\"how-to-get-featured\">How to get featured</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Pitch directly.</strong> Free and legitimate, dependent on fit and editorial capacity.</li><li><strong>Use a professional feature service.</strong> A team writes it to the publication's standard and places it. Faster and more predictable, which is why most founders choose it.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"what-makes-a-strong-piece\">What makes a strong piece</h2>\n<p>A national audience needs a reason to care that is not \"this company exists.\"</p>\n<p>The features that work here lead with something human or something surprising: the problem you set out to solve, the decision that changed the business, the thing your industry gets wrong. Broad readership rewards clarity over jargon.</p>\n<p>Write so that a reader outside your industry understands the point in the first paragraph.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-to-expect-from-the-process\">What to expect from the process</h2>\n<p>Share your story, our team drafts the piece, you review with revisions until it is exactly right, and nothing publishes until you approve it. Then it goes live and you get the link to share.</p>\n<p>Any provider who cannot show you the draft first is not one to use.</p>\n<h2 id=\"getting-started\">Getting started</h2>\n<p>Digital Networking Agency works with US Reporter and a wide network of digital publications. We write, edit and place. You keep full editorial control, and nothing goes live without your sign-off.</p>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Is US Reporter affiliated with a national news network?</h3>\n<p>No. It is an independent digital publication. Several outlets use similar names, so it is worth confirming the exact domain on any placement.</p>\n<h3>Who does US Reporter suit?</h3>\n<p>Founders and businesses whose audience spans the country rather than sitting in a single local market.</p>\n<h3>Can I approve the article before it publishes?</h3>\n<p>Yes. You review and revise until it is right, and nothing publishes without your approval.</p>",
