    "slug": "how-to-get-featured-in-international-business-times",
    "h1": "How to Get Featured in International Business Times",
    "title": "How to Get Featured in IBTimes | DNA PR",
    "description": "International Business Times covers business and markets across regional editions. What it is and how to get featured.",
    "body": "<p>If your customers, investors or partners are not all in one country, an international frame is worth more than a domestic one.</p>\n<p>Here is what International Business Times is and how people get featured.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-international-business-times-is\">What International Business Times is</h2>\n<p>International Business Times is a digital business publication covering markets, economics, companies and technology with an international perspective. Online only, permanently live, and indexed by search engines.</p>\n<p>It runs several regional editions, and what each covers differs — so the relevant question is not only whether you appear, but which edition and which audience.</p>\n<h2 id=\"why-an-international-audience-matters\">Why an international audience matters</h2>\n<p>Cross-border credibility is harder to build than domestic credibility, and it is worth more when you have it.</p>\n<p>If you are raising from overseas investors, selling into new markets, or building a business whose story is not tied to one country, coverage with an international frame does something a local feature cannot. It signals that your work is legible outside your home market.</p>\n<p>For companies with global ambitions, that framing is the point.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-a-feature-includes\">What a feature includes</h2>\n<p>A solo, dedicated article about you and your work, with a headline and angle built around your positioning. Typically photos and links to your website, LinkedIn and socials.</p>\n<p>It publishes permanently and stays indexed, becoming a reference point every time someone researches you.</p>\n<h2 id=\"how-to-get-featured\">How to get featured</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Pitch directly.</strong> Free and legitimate, dependent on fit and editorial capacity.</li><li><strong>Use a professional feature service.</strong> A team writes it to the publication's standard and places it. Faster and more predictable, which is why most founders choose it.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"what-makes-a-strong-piece\">What makes a strong piece</h2>\n<p>An international readership will not assume context.</p>\n<p>The strongest pieces explain why your work matters beyond your home market: the trend it sits inside, the problem that exists in more than one country, the numbers that make it real. Assume the reader is smart, interested and unfamiliar with your local market.</p>\n<p>Specifics travel. Local shorthand does not.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-to-expect-from-the-process\">What to expect from the process</h2>\n<p>Share your story, our team drafts the piece, you review with revisions until it is exactly right, and nothing publishes until you approve it. Then it goes live and you get the link to share.</p>\n<p>Any provider who cannot show you the draft first is not one to use.</p>\n<h2 id=\"getting-started\">Getting started</h2>\n<p>Digital Networking Agency works with International Business Times and a wide network of business publications. We write, edit and place. You keep full editorial control, and nothing goes live without your sign-off.</p>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Does it matter which edition I appear in?</h3>\n<p>Yes. The editions serve different regions and audiences, so it is worth agreeing which one fits your market before anything is written.</p>\n<h3>Who does International Business Times suit?</h3>\n<p>Companies with cross-border customers, international investors, or a story that makes sense beyond a single domestic market.</p>\n<h3>Can I approve the article before it publishes?</h3>\n<p>Yes. You review and revise until it is right, and nothing publishes without your approval.</p>",
